- The bounded-file/path test failed under PowerShell 7 and 5.1 because Test-BoundedPackageFile did not exist.
- The ICO/real-EXE test failed under both engines because Test-WindowsReferenceIcon did not exist.
- The CI YAML test failed with actual shell list [pwsh] instead of [powershell, pwsh].
- The installer diagnostic test failed under both engines because Get-NativeIconResourceFailure did not exist.
- Tests compile two real Windows PE fixtures with the .NET Framework C# compiler: one with icon.ico embedded and one without an icon. They prove the branded PE matches 32/48/256, the plain PE is refused, an ICO missing its 32 frame is refused, cleanup failure is classified runtime, and an edited interop module gets a new type identity in the same process.

